cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Controlled Feature Placement in Distillation:
  Auditing the Capacity Allocation of Superposition
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20640978
repository-code: https://github.com/PalmeseMattia/checkerboard
url: https://github.com/PalmeseMattia/checkerboard
authors:
  - given-names: Davide Mattia
    family-names: Palmese
    email: palmesedavidemattia@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A small PyTorch testbed extending Elhage et al. (2022) toy models of
  superposition and the capacity theory of Sarkar & Deka (2026). It audits
  assumption A2 of their minimum-width theorem (students keep exactly the
  top floor(d*g(alpha)) features by importance), shows the refined Eq. 2
  floor underestimates loss near and above the critical width, and that an
  equilibrium-corrected kept count restores a positive absolute-floor fit.
keywords:
  - superposition
  - knowledge distillation
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - toy models
  - capacity
